source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Cancel a run that is starting or in progress.

Cancellation is asynchronous. When the command succeeds, the server has marked
the run as cancelled, but it can still be stopping. A run that has already
completed or is incomplete cannot be cancelled: the command fails and the run
does not change.

The command needs tenant release 63.0 or newer; `snouty doctor` reports the
tenant release.

Examples:
  snouty runs cancel <run_id>

Add --json for machine-readable output. The cancelled run id prints as one JSON
object:
  snouty --json runs cancel <run_id> | jq -r .run_id

Usage: snouty runs cancel [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
